> Sudoku: a whole application in one file (spec §2). The grid (§5.1) shows
> the board and moves the cursor; digit keys run one command that gets the
> key as KEY (§9); RENDER draws the board with colors (`ansi`) when the
> program starts (`start`) and after every change.
>
>     termplate run sudoku.termplate

app SUDOKU
- termplate 0.1
- layout MAIN
- start RENDER

vars
- PUZZLE text "53..7....6..195....98....6.8...6...34..8.3..17...2...6.6....28....419..5....8..79"
- BOARD text "53..7....6..195....98....6.8...6...34..8.3..17...2...6.6....28....419..5....8..79"
- ROW number 1 range 1..9
- COL number 1 range 1..9
- VIEW text
- STATUS text

layout MAIN
bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm
bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm
bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm
bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm
bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm
bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm
bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm
bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm
bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm
bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm
bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm
bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm
bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm
sssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssss

legend:
- b GRID size.width 23 size.height 13
- m MAIN_MENU
- s STATUS_LINE size.height 2

panels
- GRID border rounded
- MAIN_MENU border rounded

> The cells are the `c` characters; the lines between the boxes are
> picture. Each value line is a row, its words the cells.
panel GRID
```
c c c │ c c c │ c c c
c c c │ c c c │ c c c
c c c │ c c c │ c c c
──────┼───────┼──────
c c c │ c c c │ c c c
c c c │ c c c │ c c c
c c c │ c c c │ c c c
──────┼───────┼──────
c c c │ c c c │ c c c
c c c │ c c c │ c c c
c c c │ c c c │ c c c
```

legend:
- c grid $VIEW ansi cursor ROW COL

panel STATUS_LINE
hhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhh
ssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssss

legend:
- h text SUDOKU.HELP
- s value $STATUS

menu MAIN_MENU
- NEW "New puzzle"
- RESTART "Start over"
- QUIT "Quit"

keys MAIN
- PUT 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 0 backspace delete
- NEW n
- quit q

text en
SUDOKU.HELP Arrows or hjkl move · 1-9 put · 0 clears · {^NEW} new game

> One command for every digit key: the key arrives as KEY.
command PUT
- env PUZZLE=$PUZZLE BOARD=$BOARD ROW=$ROW COL=$COL
- into BOARD
- then RENDER
run:
```bash
i=$(( (ROW - 1) * 9 + COL ))
case $KEY in
  [1-9]) d=$KEY ;;
  *) d=. ;;
esac
# the puzzle's own digits stay
[ "${PUZZLE:i-1:1}" != "." ] && d=${PUZZLE:i-1:1}
printf '%s' "${BOARD:0:i-1}$d${BOARD:i}"
```

> The board as nine rows of nine cells: the puzzle's digits bold, the
> player's cyan, digits that clash in a row, column or box red.
command RENDER
- env PUZZLE=$PUZZLE BOARD=$BOARD
- into VIEW
- then CHECK
run:
```bash
bad=()
for n in 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8; do
  for kind in row col box; do
    at=()
    for k in 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8; do
      case $kind in
        row) i=$(( n * 9 + k )) ;;
        col) i=$(( k * 9 + n )) ;;
        box) i=$(( (n / 3 * 3 + k / 3) * 9 + n % 3 * 3 + k % 3 )) ;;
      esac
      d=${BOARD:i:1}
      [ "$d" = . ] && continue
      if [ -n "${at[d]}" ]; then
        bad[i]=1
        bad[at[d] - 1]=1
      else
        at[d]=$(( i + 1 ))
      fi
    done
  done
done
for r in 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8; do
  line=
  for c in 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8; do
    i=$(( r * 9 + c ))
    d=${BOARD:i:1}
    if [ "$d" = . ]; then
      line+=$'\e[2m·\e[0m '
    elif [ -n "${bad[i]}" ]; then
      line+=$'\e[31m'"$d"$'\e[0m '
    elif [ "${PUZZLE:i:1}" != . ]; then
      line+=$'\e[1m'"$d"$'\e[0m '
    else
      line+=$'\e[36m'"$d"$'\e[0m '
    fi
  done
  echo "$line"
done
```

> Conflicts, the cells left, or the end of the game.
command CHECK
- env BOARD=$BOARD
- into STATUS
run:
```bash
conflicts=()
for n in 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8; do
  for kind in row col box; do
    seen=
    for k in 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8; do
      case $kind in
        row) i=$(( n * 9 + k )) ;;
        col) i=$(( k * 9 + n )) ;;
        box) i=$(( (n / 3 * 3 + k / 3) * 9 + n % 3 * 3 + k % 3 )) ;;
      esac
      d=${BOARD:i:1}
      [ "$d" = . ] && continue
      case $seen in
        *$d*) conflicts+=("$kind $(( n + 1 )): $d") ;;
      esac
      seen+=$d
    done
  done
done
if [ ${#conflicts[@]} -gt 0 ]; then
  echo "Conflict: ${conflicts[*]}"
elif [[ $BOARD != *.* ]]; then
  echo "Solved!"
else
  left=${BOARD//[^.]/}
  echo "Cells left: ${#left}"
fi
```

> A random puzzle from the list.
command NEW
- into PUZZLE
- then RESTART
run:
```bash
puzzles=(
  "53..7....6..195....98....6.8...6...34..8.3..17...2...6.6....28....419..5....8..79"
  "..3.2.6..9..3.5..1..18.64....81.29..7.......8..67.82....26.95..8..2.3..9..5.1.3.."
  "4.....8.5.3..........7......2.....6.....8.4......1.......6.3.7.5..2.....1.4......"
  ".2.6.8...58...97......4....37....5..6.......4..8....13....2......98...36...3.6.9."
)
printf '%s' "${puzzles[RANDOM % ${#puzzles[@]}]}"
```

command RESTART
- env PUZZLE=$PUZZLE
- run printf '%s' "$PUZZLE"
- into BOARD
- then RENDER
